    "heating_prelaunch_faq_Hay6C3": {
      "type": "heating-prelaunch-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_zHPpfB": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it drain my battery?",
            "answer": "<p><br/>Not while you're riding, on most bikes. With the engine running, your charging system powers the liners and tops up the battery at the same time. With both pieces on, Apex™ draws about 80W (6.67A at 12V) — roughly half what many heated sets pull.<br/><br/>To check your own bike: your stator output needs to cover what the bike already uses plus the heated gear. For example, a 300W stator with 140W of stock load leaves 160W to spare — plenty for Apex™'s 80W. A 154W heated set would fit too, but with almost nothing left over.<br/><br/>Two things to watch: on smaller or older bikes, long stretches of idling can still run the battery down, so drop to a lower level or run one piece. And never leave the heat on with the engine off — with nothing charging, it will drain the battery fast.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_jfhF4b": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I wear it without the motorcycle?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, with the 7.5K battery ($79.99, sold separately). It's built for time off the bike — walking the paddock, standing around a campsite. For riding, the 12V connection is what gives you unlimited heat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_BCPJgG": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need to buy anything else?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Each liner ships with a Y cable and a pre-sized fuse. Heat control is built into the garment — there's no controller to buy. If you want both liners running off a single lead, the 3-Way cable is needed. (sold seperately)<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_z9CMCf": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can it replace my riding jacket?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Apex™ is a mid-layer with no abrasion or impact protection. It goes under your riding gear, over a thin base layer.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
